    <div id="mainContent">
            <p class="Division"><a name="11.20.60"></a>11-20.60<br />Boundary Adjustments</p>


            <p class="digCH">Sections:</p>

            <p class="CiteTOC"><a href="../Flagstaff11/Flagstaff1120060.html#11.20.60.010">11-20.60.010</a>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Boundary Adjustments</p>

      <h3 class="Cite" id="11.20.60.010"><a name="11.20.60.010">11-20.60.010</a> Boundary Adjustments</h3>
            <p class="P1">A.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;When a common lot line between two (2) adjoining parcels requires adjustment, the submittal requirements and procedures for a land split provided in Division <a href="../Flagstaff11/Flagstaff1120050.html#11.20.50">11-20.50</a>, Land Splits or Combinations, shall be followed for review and approval by the Director.</p>

            <p class="P1">B.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;In addition to the submittal requirements for a land split or combinations established in Section <a href="../Flagstaff11/Flagstaff1120050.html#11.20.50.040">11-20.50.040</a>, Land Split and Combination Applications, the written consent of all owners of the real property associated with the proposed boundary adjustment shall be submitted. (Ord. 2024-28 (Res. 2024-45), Amended, 12/03/2024)</p>

    </div>
